btp|n|In England, formerly, the highest court of judicature next to the Parliament, exercising jurisdiction at law, but chiefly in equity; but under the jurisdiction act of 1873 it became the chancery division of the High Court of Justice, and now exercises jurisdiction only in equity. ; In the Unites States, a court of equity; equity; proceeding in equity.	a:42h,64,2~42h,64,2	n:42h,70,3~42h,70,3	N:slk,94,3~slk,94,3
